      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village grew quickly, gaining its own post office, school, and several shops and mills by the early 1800s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://kids.kiddle.co/Mount_Jackson,_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A special stage line ran through Mount Jackson to Enon Valley, making it the only way for New Castle residents to catch a train.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://kids.kiddle.co/Mount_Jackson,_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The first house in town belonged to William Henry, who also served as the first postmaster.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
